<%# What the row cannot say itself.  Replaced on every create and update — including the ones that
    succeed, which is what clears it — so a message never outlives the save that produced it.

    Both branches say the rest of the row is held, because the whole row is rejected and the reader's
    other edits are still in the form rather than in the database.  A red field on its own reads as
    "nothing was saved", which is true of the row and false of the edits. %>
<div id="transaction-message">
  <% if transaction.counterparty_to_confirm %>
    <p class="row-question">
      <strong><%= transaction.counterparty_to_confirm %></strong> is not a counterparty yet.
      Press <strong>Save</strong> on that row again to create it and save the row — or change the name
      to something else. Your other edits to the row are held until you do.
    </p>
  <% elsif transaction.errors[:counterparty_name].first.present? %>
    <p class="row-error">
      <%= transaction.errors[:counterparty_name].first %>.
      Change the name to save the row; your other edits to it are held until you do.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
